// What proves a task on the milestone branch: the test or picture that a reader can open. The
// pull request marks a task done only when its commit is on the branch and this file names the
// evidence, so a tick means the work is here and something checks it. An entry states the proof
// that exists; it does not tick the task. Some tasks still carry a recorded gap and keep their
// entry until it closes, and an entry that an audit removed stays in git history until it returns.
